\chapter{Module B: Pathogen Kinetics}

\section{Overview}

Module B models the multiscale kinetics of pathogen replication, clearance,
immune evasion, and evolutionary drift. It integrates stochastic replication
dynamics, immune system interactions, mutation-driven escape, and clinical
diagnostic assimilation.

The module is designed to:
\begin{itemize}
    \item simulate pathogen load trajectories under stochastic noise,
    \item incorporate innate and adaptive immune responses,
    \item model evolutionary escape under selective pressure,
    \item fuse clinical assay data into latent state estimates,
    \item provide downstream signals to Modules C and D.
\end{itemize}

\section{State Variables}

The pathogen-host system is represented by the state vector:
\[
\mathbf{S}_B(t)
=
\big(
P(t),\,
I(t),\,
A(t),\,
E(t)
\big),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $P(t)$: active pathogen load,
    \item $I(t)$: innate immune cell density,
    \item $A(t)$: adaptive immune capacity,
    \item $E(t)$: evolutionary escape index.
\end{itemize}

\section{Stochastic Pathogen Replication}

Pathogen replication follows a logistic SDE:
\[
dP(t)
=
\Big[
r_p P(t)
\Big(1 - \frac{P(t)}{K_p}\Big)
-
(\beta_1 A(t) + \beta_2 I(t)) P(t)
\Big] dt
+
\sigma_P \sqrt{P(t)}\, dW_t,
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $r_p$: intrinsic replication rate,
    \item $K_p$: carrying capacity,
    \item $\beta_1$: adaptive clearance coefficient,
    \item $\beta_2$: innate clearance coefficient,
    \item $\sigma_P$: stochastic noise amplitude.
\end{itemize}

\section{Innate Immune Dynamics}

Innate immunity responds rapidly:
\[
\frac{dI}{dt}
=
\alpha_I P(t)
-
\delta_I I(t),
\]
with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\alpha_I$: innate activation rate,
    \item $\delta_I$: innate decay rate.
\end{itemize}

\section{Adaptive Immune Dynamics (Neural ODE)}

Adaptive immunity is modeled using a neural ODE:
\[
\frac{dA}{dt}
=
\mathcal{NN}_{\theta}
\big(
P(t),\,
I(t),\,
A(t),\,
E(t)
\big)
-
\delta_A A(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathcal{NN}_{\theta}$: neural network parameterized by $\theta$,
    \item $\delta_A$: adaptive immune decay rate.
\end{itemize}

The neural ODE captures:
\begin{itemize}
    \item immune exhaustion,
    \item cytokine feedback loops,
    \item nonlinear activation thresholds,
    \item multi-omics-informed immune modulation.
\end{itemize}

\section{Evolutionary Escape Dynamics}

Evolutionary escape increases under selective pressure:
\[
\frac{dE}{dt}
=
\mu_{\text{mut}} P(t)
+
\lambda_E \tanh(A(t))
-
\delta_E E(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mu_{\text{mut}}$: mutation probability per replication cycle,
    \item $\lambda_E$: selective pressure coefficient,
    \item $\delta_E$: escape decay rate.
\end{itemize}

