\section{Clinical Assimilation Layer}

Clinical assays provide partial observations:
\[
\mathbf{z}_k
=
\big(
\text{NAAT}_k,\,
\text{CBC}_k
\big).
\]

Observation model:
\[
\mathbf{z}_k
=
H \mathbf{S}_B(t_k)
+
\epsilon_k,
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $H$: observation matrix,
    \item $\epsilon_k$: measurement noise.
\end{itemize}

Assimilation uses an Unscented Kalman Filter (UKF):
\[
\mathbf{S}_B(t_k^+)
=
\mathbf{S}_B(t_k^-)
+
K_k
\big(
\mathbf{z}_k - H\mathbf{S}_B(t_k^-)
\big),
\]
with $K_k$ the Kalman gain.

\section{Coupling to Module A}

Genetic dysregulation modifies:
\[
\beta_1(t)
=
\beta_1^{(0)}
+
\lambda_1 \|\mathbf{g}(t)\|,
\]
\[
\mu_{\text{mut}}(t)
=
\mu_{\text{mut}}^{(0)}
+
\lambda_2 \|\mathbf{t}(t)\|.
\]

\section{Coupling to Module C}

Trauma physiology affects:
\[
\alpha_I(t)
=
\alpha_I^{(0)}
+
\lambda_3 \iota(t),
\]
where $\iota(t)$ is the inflammatory index from Module C.

\section{Coupling to Module D}

Senescence increases susceptibility:
\[
r_p(t)
=
r_p^{(0)}
+
\lambda_4 s(t),
\]
where $s(t)$ is the senescence burden.

\section{Numerical Integration}

Hybrid solver:
\[
\mathbf{z}(t_{k+1})
=
\mathbf{z}(t_k)
+
\Delta t_k\, \Phi_B(\mathbf{z}(t_k), t_k)
+
\Sigma_B dW_t.
\]

Projection:
\[
P(t) \leftarrow \max(P(t), 0).
\]

Adaptive step control:
\[
\Delta t_{k+1}
=
\Delta t_k \cdot \psi(\epsilon_k).
\]

\section{Stress Testing}

High replication stress:
\[
r_{p,\text{stress}}
=
5 r_p^{(0)}.
\]

Immune collapse:
\[
A_{\text{stress}}(t)
=
0.1 A(t).
\]

Hypermutation:
\[
\mu_{\text{mut,stress}}
=
20 \mu_{\text{mut}}^{(0)}.
\]

\section{Module Output}

Module B outputs:
\[
\mathbf{S}_B(t)
=
\big(
P(t),\,
I(t),\,
A(t),\,
E(t)
\big),
\]
which feeds:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Module C (trauma physiology),
    \item Module D (senescence),
    \item countermeasure optimization.
\end{itemize}

\section{Summary}

Module B provides a multiscale, stochastic, immune-coupled model of pathogen
dynamics. Its integration of replication kinetics, immune response, evolutionary
escape, and clinical assimilation makes it the central engine for infection
trajectory prediction and countermeasure optimization.